; two_stage_terms.cnl — brief-wsprobe-3 R-wsp3-9(e): a two-stage amplifier between two 50 Ohm
; Terms, with the three probes the envelope of §9 wants:
;
;   PS (idx 1) sits DIRECTLY at the source Term with G facing it — node p1 carries nothing but T1,
;      so ZG(PS) = 50 exactly and the source termination is a pure shunt at PS's G node;
;   PL (idx 2) sits directly at the load Term with L facing it — node p2 carries nothing but T2;
;   P3 (idx 3) is the "suspect" internal node (stage 1's drain), the document's H03 (Eq. 187–191).
;
; P3 is declared LAST so the idx order is the document's: source = 1, load = 2, suspect = 3.
; CFB closes a global feedback loop from the input to the output, so the network is not a plain
; cascade and every wsp entry depends on both terminations.
Term:T1     p1 0   Num=1 Z=50 Ohm
WSProbe:PS  p1 s1
R:RS1   s1 g1  R=10 Ohm
C:CG1   g1 0   C=0.5 pF
R:RG1   g1 0   R=500 Ohm
VCCS:M1 d1 0  g1 0  G=0.04
R:RO1   d1 0   R=400 Ohm
C:CD1   d1 0   C=0.3 pF
L:L12   d1x g2 L=2 nH
C:CG2   g2 0   C=0.4 pF
R:RG2   g2 0   R=300 Ohm
VCCS:M2 d2 0  g2 0  G=0.05
R:RO2   d2 0   R=300 Ohm
C:CF2   g2 d2  C=0.1 pF
C:CFB   s1 d2  C=0.05 pF
L:L2    d2 a2  L=1.5 nH
WSProbe:PL  a2 p2
Term:T2     p2 0   Num=2 Z=50 Ohm
WSProbe:P3  d1 d1x
analysis SP1 type=sparam start=1 stop=3 npts=21 Unit=GHz
